Project Planning

1. Project Goal

The main goal of ComicCraft is to develop an AI-powered application that helps users create comic story content using Gemini models.

2. Development Plan

Phase 1 – Brainstorming

Identify the problem and select the project idea.

Phase 2 – Requirement Analysis

Identify the required hardware, software, and application requirements.

Phase 3 – Project Design

Design the architecture, workflow, and user interface.

Phase 4 – Project Development

Develop the application and integrate the Gemini model.

Phase 5 – Testing

Test the application using different prompts and identify errors.

Phase 6 – Documentation

Prepare the project report and supporting documents.

Phase 7 – Demonstration

Demonstrate the working application and explain the project.

3. Task Allocation

The project activities include:

- Project research
- Requirement analysis
- UI development
- Backend development
- Gemini integration
- Testing
- Documentation
- Demonstration

4. Expected Deliverables

- Working ComicCraft application
- Source code
- Design documents
- Testing report
- Project documentation
- Demonstration video
- Public GitHub repository

Conclusion

The project planning phase provides a structured approach for completing ComicCraft. Dividing the project into different tasks and phases helps the team complete the project systematically and efficiently.